# Wave W17-AA (Route 221): tide sand — the coast path’s pale sand, design-authorised: a pale cool sand running the shore from the long sea’s landfall north to Fenland’s gate, carrying sparse shell-pale flecks the tide left in its tread (design: rock-ringed tide pools keep tiny worlds along the shore; the path keeps what the tide leaves). Split from Route 222’s solar sand by coolth entire (tide-pale vs sun-bleached) and from Route 219’s bright sand by element: this sand is walked on, that sand is waded over.
